WEBVTT
NOTE SYNC_TYPE: HUMAN_VERIFIED
NOTE Track: 1-05 - The Weighted Blankets
NOTE Artist: Crimson Node
NOTE Album: 2002: Crimson Node

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.000
[Instrumental Intro: Rhythmic Tom Drums, Driving Bassline & Siren Synth]

00:00:29.334 --> 00:00:32.800
Seventy pounds of tactical grace

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:36.200
Running the perimeter, securing the space

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:39.800
The instigator wedges right into the fold

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:43.500
While the stoic anchor comes in from the cold

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:47.200
We've got a riot squad pacing the floor

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:50.800
Waiting for the signal right outside the door

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:54.486
When the system starts flashing and the circuits overload

00:00:54.526 --> 00:00:58.500
They are running down the hallway, they are taking up the road

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:02.288
Bring in the heavy weight, the gravity we need

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:06.552
A living blanket to slow down the speed

00:01:06.572 --> 00:01:10.500
When the static is screaming and the processor is trapped

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:15.500
We are safely anchored, perfectly wrapped

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:21.525
Yeah, we are safely anchored, perfectly wrapped!

00:01:24.118 --> 00:01:27.941
Down by the jungle room, the siren starts to wail

00:01:28.381 --> 00:01:31.322
Arguing with shadows, chasing her own tail

00:01:31.382 --> 00:01:34.800
A screaming match echoing straight through the wall

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:38.326
With the apex predator refusing to fall

00:01:38.406 --> 00:01:42.068
It's an acoustic war in the middle of the night

00:01:42.128 --> 00:01:46.200
But it tells the central processor that everything is right

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:49.652
When the system starts flashing and the circuits overload

00:01:49.672 --> 00:01:53.800
They are running down the hallway, they are taking up the road

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:58.000
Bring in the heavy weight, the gravity we need

00:01:58.029 --> 00:02:01.789
A living blanket to slow down the speed

00:02:01.809 --> 00:02:05.800
When the static is screaming and the processor is trapped

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:10.500
We are safely anchored, perfectly wrapped

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:16.532
Yeah, we are safely anchored, perfectly wrapped!

00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:26.800
Deep pressure on the mat.

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:30.200
The panic fades to black.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:35.200
We build a fortress on the floor, and we are coming back.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:38.982
We are coming back!

00:02:39.200 --> 00:03:07.500
[Guitar Solo]

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:12.501
Bring in the heavy weight, the gravity we need

00:03:12.541 --> 00:03:15.462
A living blanket to slow down the speed

00:03:15.482 --> 00:03:19.000
When the static is screaming and the processor is trapped

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:22.865
We are safely anchored, perfectly wrapped

00:03:28.366 --> 00:03:31.500
The acoustic war.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:34.800
The weighted blanket.

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:38.743
System stabilized.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:51.000
[Outro]
